  exhibitName: 'General Electric ES44AC Black '
  description: "United States, Early 21st Century \n\nThis locomotive is part of
    the Evolution Series, a landmark family of diesel-electric engines developed
    by General Electric to meet the environmental and efficiency standards of the
    21st century. Introduced in the mid-2000s, the ES44AC became one of the most
    widely used freight locomotives across North America, valued for its 4,400-horsepower
    output, AC traction technology, and reduced emissions compared to earlier models.
    \n\nFeaturing a wide-cab design, reinforced frame, and advanced dynamic braking
    systems, the ES44AC was engineered for long-distance heavy freight operations
    on major railroads. Its GEVO-12 prime mover represented a significant step forward
    in cleaner-burning diesel technology, marking a turning point in the shift toward
    more sustainable rail transport. "
